+
+# Newsletter discount codes (SPRING10, WELCOME5)
+
+Spring campaign: customers receive discount codes in the newsletter, and an order can take one.
+
+## What the order book must do
+
+- `applyCode(orderNumber, code)` gives an order a discount code.
+- `SPRING10` takes 10 % off the order's items, rounded to the nearest cent (a half cent rounds up).
+- `WELCOME5` takes 5.00 EUR (500 cents) off the order's items, and only on an order whose items come to 30.00 EUR
+  (3000 cents) or more.
+- An order takes one code at most; a second code replaces the first.
+- An unknown code, or `WELCOME5` on a smaller order, is refused with an error that says why, and the order is left
+  as it was.
+- The discount never touches shipping. Whether an order ships free is decided on its items before any discount.
+- An order's totals show the discount as `discountCents` (0 without a code), and `totalCents` is items minus
+  discount plus shipping.
+
+## Traceability
+
+- Feature: newsletter discount codes for the spring campaign.
+- Requirement: the code rules above, in integer cents.
+- Acceptance: the cases listed above, each covered by a test in `test/`.
+
+## Implementation
+
+- `src/domain/discounts.ts`: the two codes and `discountFor(code, itemsCents)`, integer arithmetic only; SPRING10
+  rounds half up with `floor((items * 10 + 50) / 100)`; WELCOME5 is refused below 3000 cents of items.
+- `src/domain/orders.ts`: `applyCode(number, code)` computes the discount on the items before any discount, stores
+  it on the order as `discount` (code and cents) and replaces any earlier one; a refused code leaves the order as
+  it was. `totals` reports `discountCents` (0 without a code) and `totalCents = items - discount + shipping`.
+  Shipping is still decided by `shippingFor` on the undiscounted lines.
+- `src/index.ts`: exports the `AppliedDiscount` type.
+- `test/shop.test.ts`: 9 new tests of the discount rules (happy path, rounding, shipping, boundaries, refusals,
+  replacement); the existing totals test now expects `discountCents: 0`. `npm test`: 14 of 14 pass.
+- Not changed: `package.json` version and `CHANGELOG.md` (a release follows approval).
